{title: A Low Whisper}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 17:1–16; 18:20–39; 19:3–13; 2 Kings 2:11–12}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 91}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] |
| [Gm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Elijah stood before King Ahab, said no dew and no rain
Elijah stood before King Ahab, said no dew and no rain
Then [C]the ravens brought him bread and meat, morning and [Gm]evening again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Down in Zarephath a widow had one handful of flour
Down in Zarephath a widow had one handful of flour
But the [C]jar did not run out and the oil kept pouring [Gm]every hour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
How long will you keep limping between two opinions, he said
Four hundred fifty prophets danced and shouted till the day was dead
He soaked the wood three times [C]with water, filled the trench up to the brim
Then the fire of [Gm]the LORD came down [D7]and licked it up for him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD, he is God
The [Gm]LORD, he is God
Fire fell on Car[C]mel and the people cried
The [Gm]LORD, he is God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Then he ran [D7]from Jezebel and lay down underneath a broom bush
Said, E[Gm]nough, LORD, take my life; I am no better than my fathers
But an angel touched him, get up and eat, a loaf on burning stones
Forty days and forty nights he walked to [C]Horeb all alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Not in the wind
Not in the earthquake
[D7]Not in the fire
But the sound of a little whisper
What are you doing here, Elijah?
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]The LORD, he is God
The LORD, [Gm]he is God
Fire fell on Car[D]mel and the people cried
The LORD, he is God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
A char[Gm]iot of fire and horses of fire
He went up to heaven in a whirlwind
My father! My father!
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
